  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of three-digit numbers, with one digit repeated exactly two times, is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "243",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For three digit number we have following cases,</p><p><strong>Case I:</strong> When digit zero is repeated</p><p>Number of numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><strong>Case II:</strong> When digit zero is present but not repeated</p><p>Number of numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p><p><strong>Case III:</strong> When digit zero is not present</p><p>Number of numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>216</mn></math></p><p>Total number of numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>243</mn></math></p>",
